=== SIGNATURE ===
z_route_edges_candidates(costs, frontier, board, move_rule, dir_list, row_delta, col_delta, infinity)

=== COMMENT ===
Private helper for route_edges; do not call directly. Returns all valid cost improvements reachable from the current frontier.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(costs, frontier, board, move_rule, dir_list, row_delta, col_delta, infinity,
  LET(
    row_count, ROWS(board),
    col_count, COLUMNS(board),
    dir_count, ROWS(dir_list),
    source_count, ROWS(frontier),
    source_rows, INDEX(frontier, 0, 1),
    source_cols, INDEX(frontier, 0, 2),
    source_costs, INDEX(frontier, 0, 3),
    target_rows, TOCOL(source_rows + TRANSPOSE(row_delta)),
    target_cols, TOCOL(source_cols + TRANSPOSE(col_delta)),
    base_costs, TOCOL(source_costs + SEQUENCE(, dir_count, 0, 0)),
    valid_targets, (target_rows >= 1) * (target_rows <= row_count) * (target_cols >= 1) * (target_cols <= col_count),
    safe_rows, MAP(target_rows, LAMBDA(row_ix, MIN(row_count, MAX(1, row_ix)))),
    safe_cols, MAP(target_cols, LAMBDA(col_ix, MIN(col_count, MAX(1, col_ix)))),
    from_cells, TOCOL(MAKEARRAY(
      source_count,
      dir_count,
      LAMBDA(row_ix, dir_ix, INDEX(board, INDEX(source_rows, row_ix), INDEX(source_cols, row_ix)))
    )),
    to_cells, MAP(safe_rows, safe_cols, LAMBDA(row_ix, col_ix, INDEX(board, row_ix, col_ix))),
    dir_values, TOCOL(MAKEARRAY(
      source_count,
      dir_count,
      LAMBDA(row_ix, dir_ix, INDEX(dir_list, dir_ix))
    )),
    edge_costs, MAP(
      from_cells,
      to_cells,
      dir_values,
      LAMBDA(from_cell, to_cell, dir, IFNA(move_rule(from_cell, to_cell, dir), infinity))
    ),
    clean_edges, MAP(
      edge_costs,
      LAMBDA(edge, IF(NOT(ISNUMBER(edge)), infinity, IF(edge < 0, infinity, edge)))
    ),
    candidate_costs, MAP(base_costs, clean_edges, LAMBDA(base_cost, edge, MIN(infinity, base_cost + edge))),
    IF(
      valid_targets * (candidate_costs < INDEX(costs, safe_rows, safe_cols)),
      HSTACK(target_rows, target_cols, candidate_costs),
      {0, 0, 0}
    )
  )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Private candidate-generation helper for route_edges.

For every cell in the current frontier, it constructs the allowed neighboring moves, calls move_rule(from_cell, to_cell, dir), and returns {row, column, cost} for moves that improve the destination's current cost. Out-of-bounds moves, #N/A, text, and negative move costs are treated as illegal. Other Excel errors remain visible.

Arguments:
  costs       - current least-known cost array.
  frontier    - rows of {row, column, cost} whose outgoing moves must be examined.
  board       - map/helper array passed to move_rule.
  move_rule   - LAMBDA(from_cell, to_cell, dir) returning a legal nonnegative edge cost or NA()/text/negative for an illegal edge.
  dir_list    - allowed direction arrows.
  row_delta   - row offset corresponding to each direction.
  col_delta   - column offset corresponding to each direction.
  infinity    - numeric sentinel used for unreachable cells and illegal moves.

Returns:
  Rows of {destination row, destination column, proposed cost}. Non-improving and illegal candidates are represented by zero rows for the worker to discard.
